---
title: Nested Multi-Layer Script Obfuscation Execution
id: 4f6a7b8c-9d1e-4f3a-b2c3-5d6e7f8a9b04
status: experimental
description: Detects PowerShell or script execution with multiple chained encoding/decoding layers, consistent with Lazarus's reported Matryoshka-style nested obfuscation used to evade signature-based tooling.
author: Dalton Hunter
date: 2026/08/23
references:
    - https://www.group-ib.com/masked-actors/lazarus/
tags:
    - attack.defense_evasion
    - attack.t1027
    - attack.t1140
logsource:
    category: process_creation
    product: windows
detection:
    selection:
        Image|endswith: '\powershell.exe'
        CommandLine|contains|all:
            - '-EncodedCommand'
    selection_nested:
        CommandLine|contains:
            - 'FromBase64String'
            - 'IEX'
    condition: selection and selection_nested
falsepositives:
    - Legitimate admin scripts using encoded commands for special characters, though nested decode chains are uncommon
level: high

